<title>NORWAY: Norway may invest oil wealth in foreign shares.</title>
<headline>Norway may invest oil wealth in foreign shares.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Norway, the world's second biggest oil exporter after Saudi Arabia, said on Tuesday it may invest 30 to 50 percent of the state Petroleum Fund in overseas stock exchanges.</p>
<p>Norway, which has run up a budget surplus for three consecutive years, has so far invested the surplus in low-risk foreign government bonds only.</p>
</text>
